1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,098
Dr. Fright, the Dream Doctor: he hunts you in your nightmares, and the burns are

2
00:00:04,098 --> 00:00:05,143
real when you wake up.

3
00:00:05,363 --> 00:00:06,643
Here's how he plays.

4
00:00:07,467 --> 00:00:12,090
Shuffle the four Boiler Room cards face down, and put the Awake/Asleep card on top,

5
00:00:12,090 --> 00:00:14,485
Awake side up. That's the Boiler Room deck.

6
00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:19,132
You start Awake. While Awake you play as normal, but he can't attack you and you

7
00:00:19,132 --> 00:00:22,532
can't attack him. If a Victim is in his space, he'll still attack them.

8
00:00:22,752 --> 00:00:26,720
You fall Asleep when a card says so, or by choice with a Short or Long Rest.

9
00:00:27,533 --> 00:00:31,182
Asleep, you're in his Boiler Room. You can move, search and attack him, and he

10
00:00:31,182 --> 00:00:32,632
resolves his attacks as normal.

11
00:00:32,852 --> 00:00:36,821
Victims won't follow you and can't be saved, and you must resolve one Boiler Room

12
00:00:36,821 --> 00:00:38,633
card at the end of each Killer phase.

13
00:00:39,467 --> 00:00:43,182
Slide the deck up, down, left or right to reveal part of the next card.

14
00:00:43,182 --> 00:00:46,165
If Dr. Fright is showing, he attacks you, wherever he is.

15
00:00:46,385 --> 00:00:49,603
He appears in each quadrant only once, so track what you've seen.

16
00:00:49,603 --> 00:00:51,484
Reveal all four cards and you wake up.

17
00:00:52,300 --> 00:00:55,244
A few tips. Do your rescues while Awake, and choose when to sleep.

18
00:00:55,464 --> 00:00:59,089
Keeping Victims alive keeps his Bloodlust low and him nearly still.

19
00:00:59,089 --> 00:01:00,712
The Megaphone is a great find.

20
00:01:00,932 --> 00:01:04,954
He's one of the easier killers: about three wins in four on Final Girl Stats.

21
00:01:04,954 --> 00:01:05,476
Good luck.

